{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310669,"nonce":"5nDkD9PQDxT9eM3xRDZTStPCDYc=","title":"THREE HOLES FIXED 3df9e77a + 14c8ed09 (@:manualDrop delivered; @:move now unsuppressable by @:safety or by bundle/AOT). REMAINING: the ...","message":"**CORRECTION 2026-08-19.** An earlier version of this note said the ownership\nanalysis \"never runs\". **That was wrong** and is corrected below. There are TWO\nseparate implementations; one is dead, the other is live and does reject code.\n\n\n`CompilationUnit::check_ownership_violations` (compilation.rs:7979) builds an\n`OwnershipGraph` and is called from compilation.rs:6445, gated:\n\n```rust\nlet has_safety_opt_out = typed_file.classes.iter().any(|c| c.has_safety_annotation());\nif !is_stdlib \u0026\u0026 self.config.emit_safety_warnings \u0026\u0026 !has_safety_opt_out {\n```\n\n`@:move` violations are HARD ERRORS. **Verified empirically**: a `@:move class\nBox` with `var b = a; use(a)` is rejected by `rayzor run` with\n`[E0382] use of moved value: 'a'`.\n\n\n`HaxeCompilationPipeline::run_memory_safety_analysis` — which drives\n`OwnershipAnalyzer` (pipeline.rs:2826) and `LifetimeAnalyzer` (pipeline.rs:3002)\n— is **never invoked by the driver**: `grep -c 'self\\.pipeline\\b'\ncompiler/src/compilation.rs` = **0**. Reachable only from tests,\n`pipeline_validation.rs`, `bin/validate_pipeline.rs`. An env-gated `eprintln!`\nprobe at that call site printed NOTHING on a real nue build.\n`lower_to_tast`'s doc comment claiming it delegates there is STALE.\nThose analyzers pass 9/9 unit tests but only on HAND-BUILT graphs.\n\n\n**1. BUNDLE AND AOT DISABLE ENFORCEMENT ENTIRELY.** `emit_safety_warnings =\nfalse` at `codegen/aot_compiler.rs:96` and `tools/preblade.rs:80` (the bundle\npath). **Verified empirically**: the identical file that `rayzor run` rejects\nwith a hard error gives `Bundle created` under `rayzor bundle`, and running that\nbundle PRINTS `1 1` — the use-after-move executes. Everything nue ships is\nbundled, so nothing we ship is checked.\n\n**2. `@:safety` INVERTS THE GATE.** `has_safety_opt_out` is true if ANY class in\nthe file carries `@:safety`, which disables ownership checking for the WHOLE\nFILE. But node.rs:333 documents `@:move` as \"**Requires @:safety on the class**\".\n**Following the documentation turns the check off.** Verified empirically: adding\nan unrelated `@:safety(false) class Other {}` to the rejected file made it\ncompile and print `1 1`.\n\n**3. `@:manualDrop` IS A BROKEN CHAIN — DOUBLE-FREE VECTOR.** It parses\n(`\"manualDrop\" =\u003e Some(MemoryAnnotation::ManualDrop)`, node.rs:411) and MIR\nconsumes it (metadata.rs:535 fills `manual_drop_classes`, lookups.rs:219 reads\nit), but `tast_to_hir.rs:623-627` whitelists only Move/Managed/Shared and drops\neverything else via `_ =\u003e None`. So `manual_drop_classes` is PERMANENTLY EMPTY\nand an annotated class silently falls through to `DropBehavior::AutoDrop` —\nthe compiler frees a value the user was told to free themselves.\n\n\n`OwnershipGraph::check_use_after_move` (semantic_graph/ownership_graph.rs:551-581)\ncompares SOURCE POSITIONS:\n`use_loc.line \u003e move_loc.line || (same line \u0026\u0026 use_loc.column \u003e move_loc.column)`,\nthen `break` after the first violation per variable. No CFG, no branch or loop\nawareness, no \"reassignment revives the binding\". So it is BOTH unsound and\nincomplete: a use textually before a move inside a loop body is missed; a use in\na not-taken branch, or after a genuine reassignment, is falsely flagged.\nThis is the LIVE path — `check_ownership_violations` calls exactly this.\n\n\n- `MarkMoved` is emitted at exactly ONE site (mir/stmt/statements.rs:397-402),\n  covering only the `var b = a;` shape — not calls, `return a`, plain\n  assignment, or field stores. `strict_move_locals` is cleared at every\n  function/lambda/vtable/init boundary, so tracking never crosses a call.\n- `Send` is opt-OUT: `auto_derive_send` (trait_checker.rs:290-297) returns true\n  when every field is Send, vacuously true for a field-less class — contradicting\n  the \"type does not derive Send\" error text.\n- `Thread.spawn` Send checking only inspects a LITERAL closure passed directly as\n  the first argument (send_sync_validator.rs:152-158); a closure passed through a\n  variable is unchecked, as is any capture whose type failed to resolve.\n- `Channel\u003cT\u003e`/`Arc\u003cT\u003e` element constraints are checked only at `new`, never at\n  call sites; the expression walk silently ignores unenumerated kinds.\n- The Send/Sync path never calls `extend_classes`, so it does not see stdlib\n  TypedClasses (contrast compilation.rs:8036-8038 on the ownership path).\n\n\n| backend | MarkMoved / CheckLive |\n|---|---|\n| Cranelift | ENFORCED — per-IrId liveness slots + `rayzor_panic_use_after_move` |\n| **LLVM** | **no-op** (llvm_jit_backend.rs:5666) — this is the AOT/release tier |\n| interpreter | no-op unless `RAYZOR_STRICT_MOVE_CHECK` (mir_interpreter.rs:1073) |\n| C / wasm | no-op / no arm at all |\n\n\n1. **Close hole 1** — bundle/AOT must not silently disable safety. One-line\n   flags; the question is what SHOULD be enforced there, not how.\n2. **Close hole 2** — `@:safety` must not mean \"disable checking\" while the docs\n   call it a prerequisite. Decide which meaning is intended and make both agree.\n3. **Fix hole 3** — forward ManualDrop through the tast_to_hir whitelist.\n4. Only then: replace the textual comparison with real dataflow, and decide\n   whether to revive the (better, unit-tested) dead analyzers instead.\n\n---\n\n\n- **3df9e77a** — `tast_to_hir` now forwards `ManualDrop` (match made EXHAUSTIVE,\n  no `_` arm, so a new annotation cannot be silently dropped again). Verified by\n  reading the chain; a runtime A/B could NOT witness it because scalar\n  replacement elides the allocation in any small program that would show it.\n- **14c8ed09** — `@:move` violations are now unsuppressable. `@:safety` and\n  `emit_safety_warnings` (cleared by bundle+AOT) now filter ADVISORY diagnostics\n  only; severity decides. Verified: `rayzor bundle MoveA.hx` now fails and emits\n  no artifact; `@:safety(false) class Other {}` no longer lets it through.\n  184/184; nue bundles with identical tokens; bundle 3.3s.\n- NOTE: deltablue stack-overflows AT RUNTIME (`Running deltablue.hx` prints\n  first, so it compiles). Pre-existing, unrelated to these fixes, NOT in the\n  184 suite.\n\n\n- **10 of 14 memory annotations are inert**: `Unique`, `Borrow`, `Owned`,\n  `Linear`, `Affine`, `Box`, `Arc`, `Atomic`, `Rc`, `Managed` reach NO consumer.\n  Only `Move`, `Shared` (metadata.rs:401), and now `ManualDrop` do anything.\n- **Borrows are never emitted.** `BorrowImmutable`/`BorrowMutable` appear only in\n  passes that MATCH them (optimization.rs:904, bounds_check_elimination.rs:278,\n  dump.rs:157). No construction site exists. `enable_borrow_checking` is read\n  nowhere. There is no borrow checking of any kind.\n- **`MarkMoved` fires at ONE syntactic form.** statements.rs:392-405, inside\n  `VarDeclaration` only, and only when the initializer is a bare `Variable`. So\n  `var b = a;` is tracked; `b = a;`, `f(a)`, `return a;`, `this.x = a;`,\n  `arr.push(a)` are ALL untracked.\n- **The live checker is textual** (ownership_graph.rs:551-581): line/column\n  comparison, `break` after the first hit per variable. No CFG, branches, loops,\n  or reassignment-revives ⇒ unsound AND incomplete.\n- **Only Cranelift enforces at runtime**; LLVM (the shipping tier) no-ops\n  `MarkMoved`/`CheckLive`.\n- **Send/Sync holes**: `Mutex\u003cT\u003e` is Sync with no `T: Send` bound;\n  `MutexGuard.get()` lets the inner reference escape the guard; `Thread.spawn`\n  checks only a LITERAL closure argument; `Channel`/`Arc` checked only at `new`;\n  the Send/Sync path never calls `extend_classes` so it cannot see stdlib types.\n\n\nRayzor's REAL memory model today is **automatic drop insertion**\n(`insert_free`/`drop_analysis`) — RAII-like, not affine. The annotation\nvocabulary advertises an affine/borrow model that does not exist. Inert\nannotations are WORSE than absent: a user annotates `@:unique` and believes it.\n\nSuggested order if the goal is \"no GC ⇒ real safety tools\":\n1. Make the path that actually runs SOUND — `insert_free` has produced repeated\n   real miscompiles ([[bugs_loop_body_class_alloc_never_freed]],\n   [[bugs_string_concat_in_loop_double_free]],\n   [[bugs_release_guard_blind_to_call_shaped_frees]]). This is load-bearing today.\n2. Make Send/Sync sound — it gates the concurrency work\n   ([[project_multispoke_pool_not_the_blocker]]) and its bounds are currently\n   unchecked promises.\n3. THEN decide affine/borrow: either implement it (the dead\n   `semantic_graph` analyzers are better than the live checker and pass 9/9, but\n   have never seen a real graph) or DELETE the unbacked vocabulary.\n\n\nUSER'S INTENDED MODEL (their words): the annotations that matter are **Borrow,\nOwned, Box, Arc, Atomic, Rc**. `Managed` is DEPRECATED — it was an opt-in GC\nalternative and is no longer wanted. (NOTE: `Box` and `Atomic` are `extern abstract`, `Arc` is `extern class` — grep for `extern class` alone MISSES two of them. `Linear`/`Affine` are NOT GPU-related:\nzero uses in any .hx, the WGSL transpiler has no ownership awareness, and\n`implies_move_semantics()` — which lists them — is itself never called.)\n\nI had conflated \"annotation has no consumer\" with \"capability absent\". Verified:\n\n| | type exists | annotation wired | reality |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Arc | `rayzor/concurrent/Arc.hx` | `@:arc` inert | **`@:shared` ALREADY IS THIS** — emits `rayzor_\u003cClass\u003e_arc_clone` (metadata.rs:486), atomic RC, explicitly the opposite of `@:move` (metadata.rs:410), and `requires_shared` is consulted (compilation.rs:8082) |\n| Atomic | `rayzor/Atomic.hx` — `extern abstract`, carries `@:derive([Send])` | `@:atomic` inert | type is real and load-bearing (SpinPool control cells) |\n| Box | `rayzor/Box.hx` — `extern abstract` | `@:box` inert | real wrapper type (`init`/`unbox`/`as_ptr`) |\n| **Rc** | **NONE — verified absent** | inert | **REAL GAP.** No `.hx` mentions `Rc`, no `rayzor::Rc` runtime symbol. Single-threaded sharing must pay ATOMIC refcount via `@:shared`. (Owner believed it existed — confirm it is not uncommitted before building.) |\n| **Borrow** | **none** | inert | **THE GAP** — `BorrowImmutable`/`BorrowMutable` exist in MIR but have NO construction site anywhere; only matched by optimization.rs:904 / bce.rs:278 / dump.rs:157 |\n| Owned | none | inert | arguably the implicit default |\n\nSo the gap is TWO capabilities, not ten annotations:\n\n1. **Borrow** — needs an emission site, then checking. This is where\n   `MutexGuard.get()` escaping the guard, Tensor views aliasing their storage,\n   and `KVCache` handed across a call all live.\n2. **Rc** — a NON-atomic sibling of `@:shared`. Cheap given `@:shared` exists\n   (same machinery, non-atomic increment) BUT its safety rests on `Rc` being\n   `!Send`, which the Send/Sync checker cannot express soundly today\n   (`auto_derive_send` grants Send by field inspection; `Mutex\u003cT\u003e` is Sync with\n   no `T: Send` bound). **So Rc depends on the Send/Sync fixes that\n   [[project_multispoke_pool_not_the_blocker]] also needs.**\n3. Housekeeping: wire `@:arc`/`@:box`/`@:atomic` to the implementations that\n   already exist, or delete the spellings so they cannot mislead. Drop `Managed`.\n\n\n**Owner: \"we started a memory model plan and stopped half-way, hence the many\ninert/absent.\"** So this is an UNFINISHED PLAN, not accumulated dead vocabulary.\nRead that doc FIRST before proposing anything; also\n`memory_safety_implementation.md` (374) and `memory_safety_wiki.md` (843).\n\n**WHY OPT-IN (owner):** to support legacy Haxe-ecosystem libraries, which alias\nfreely and assume a GC. Unannotated code must be analysed NOT AT ALL — not\nanalysed-and-forgiven. That constraint is load-bearing on every design choice.\n\nSpec: default = runtime-managed, no analysis. `@:safety` enrols. `@:safety(true)`\n= Strict (every class must be annotated). Parameter-level `@:borrow` / `@:owned`\n/ `@:move` are specified too — and `TypedParameter` has NO annotation field, so\nparameter-level annotations are UNIMPLEMENTED end to end.\n\n\nWas inverted (annotation suppressed the file). Advisories now require opt-in;\n`@:move` stays a hard error everywhere. Verified: unannotated nue went from\n**104 advisories to 0**; `@:move` still errors on run AND blocks `bundle`;\n`@:safety` no longer hides it. 184/184, nue tokens identical.\n\n\nThose 104 were FALSE POSITIVES. Example (BPETokenizer.hx): `return\nencodeBPE(text);` at :121 flagged as moving `text`, then `text.length` at :126\nreported as use-after-move — but :126 is only reachable when the return at :121\nwas NOT taken. `check_use_after_move` compares SOURCE POSITIONS only. It also\ntreats a call argument as a move regardless of type (`text` is a `String`, which\nthe trait checker itself calls Clone), and it flagged 20 sites in Q4Matmul.hx,\n8 in LlamaArch.hx. **Turning advisories on for annotated code would bury real\nfindings.** The dead `semantic_graph` analyzers (9/9 tests, CFG + constraint\nsolver + inter-procedural per the doc) are the intended replacement.\n\n\n| spec item | state |\n|---|---|\n| `@:safety` opt-in | FIXED 8184206b |\n| `@:move` | enforced, unsuppressable (14c8ed09) |\n| `@:manualDrop` | delivered (3df9e77a) |\n| `@:arc` | inert — but `@:shared` already implements it |\n| `@:rc` | **omitted by the owner**; no `Rc` type exists |\n| `@:unique` | inert |\n| `@:borrow` / `@:owned` (param-level) | **unimplemented**: no field on `TypedParameter`, and `BorrowImmutable`/`BorrowMutable` have NO emission site |\n| ownership analysis | live one is textual/false-positive-heavy; good one is dead |\n| lifetime analysis / constraint solver | dead (never invoked) |\n| drop analysis | LIVE — `insert_free`, the load-bearing piece |\n| escape analysis | `ir/escape_analysis.rs` — liveness unverified |\n| Send/Sync | live but unsound (see above) |\n\n\n`f(a); g(a)` — a genuine double-move of an `Array` — produces **NO diagnostic**.\nRoot cause, traced end to end:\n\n- Every call argument that is a bare `Variable` is recorded as a MOVE\n  (compilation.rs FunctionCall/MethodCall/StaticMethodCall arms, `MoveType::FunctionCall`)\n  **and** as a USE (`record_use` in the `Variable` arm, compilation.rs:8286) — at\n  the SAME `source_location`.\n- `check_use_after_move` considers only the LAST move (`node.move_site`) and\n  requires a use STRICTLY after it (`use.line \u003e move.line || same line \u0026\u0026 col \u003e`).\n- So the final mention of a variable is simultaneously the last move and a use at\n  identical coordinates ⇒ the comparison is false ⇒ nothing is reported.\n\nIt therefore fires ONLY when a bare non-argument read appears textually after the\nlast argument-position mention (`takeStr(s)` then `s + n`), and misses the common\n`f(a); g(a)` entirely. **Unsound in both directions**, on top of having no branch\nor loop awareness. `record_use` has exactly ONE live caller.\n`OwnershipGraph::record_use` is otherwise called only from the DEAD pipeline\n(pipeline.rs:2111) and from tests.\n\nCONCLUSION: this checker cannot be the foundation for `@:borrow`/`@:owned`.\nWiring a package-wide safety switch (rayzor.toml) to it would scale a detector\nthat is wrong in both directions.\n\n\n- String: not Copy (owns a heap buffer) but IS Clone and immutable — reading it\n  cannot consume it. Filter now accepts Copy OR Clone. `@:move` still wins.\n- Unresolved variable type skipped the filter entirely and fell through to a\n  report; a resolution gap arrived as a use-after-move accusation. Now skipped.\n- MEASURED: Int/Float/Bool/Array were ALREADY quiet (Copy filter, and Array via\n  the cancellation above — NOT by exemption; `implements_trait` has no Array arm,\n  so Array is neither Copy nor Clone).\n\n\n1. **rayzor.toml package-wide safety**, honored for the package but NOT external\n   deps. Manifest already models `dependencies` separately from\n   `build.class_paths` (workspace/manifest.rs:57-83), and `is_stdlib_source`\n   (compilation.rs:1190) is the existing path-prefix boundary — so the\n   package/dep split has a foundation. NOT IMPLEMENTED. Blocked on the checker\n   being worth scaling.\n2. Parameter-level `@:borrow`/`@:owned`: `TypedParameter` (node.rs:190) has NO\n   annotation field — unimplemented from the parser down.\n\n\n`var a = new Res(1); var b = a; var d = b; Sys.println(d.v);` with a `@:move`\nclass: LLVM prints 1, **Cranelift traps** `use-after-move: d was already moved`.\n\nMIR dump shows why:\n```\n$2 = call fn0($1)      // a\nCheckLive $2 (line 6)  // read a\n$9 = cast *u8 $2       // relocation for the bind\nMarkMoved $2           // a moved\nCheckLive $9 (line 7)  // read b  -\u003e b IS $9\nMarkMoved $9           // b moved\nCheckLive $9 (line 8)  // read d  -\u003e d IS $9 TOO\n```\n`var d = b` needs NO cast, so `d` and `b` share a register.\n`strict_move_locals.insert(final_value)` registered it for `d`, then\n`MarkMoved(src_reg)` poisoned it for `b`. FIXED by emitting MarkMoved only when\n`src_reg != final_value`. Genuine violations still trap and still fail to\ncompile. 184/184, nue tokens identical.\n\n**THE GENERAL LESSON: liveness is keyed on REGISTERS, the property is about\nBINDINGS.** Two bindings sharing a register cannot be told apart. Any future\nchecker MUST be keyed on SymbolId, not IrId. (Also note `IrInstruction::uses()`\nreturns `[src]` for BOTH MarkMoved and CheckLive, so a MIR use/def scan would\nre-import the move-and-use-at-the-same-point cancellation that already kills the\nTAST checker.)\n\n\nSame file, same move, only the trailing expression varied:\n| expression | diagnostics |\n|---|---|\n| `Sys.println(a.v + \" \" + b.v)` | **3** |\n| `Sys.println(a.v)` | **0** |\n| `Sys.println(a.v + b.v)` | **0** |\nDetection depends on the shape of the surrounding expression, not on the move.\nConclusive: REPLACE, do not patch.\n\n\n5 cases with declared ERROR/SILENT expectations + `check.sh`. Deliberately NOT\nunder `compiler/tests/haxe/` (which the 184-suite globs and scores by exit code).\n**Baseline 3/5.** c1_double_move and c3_loop are the two that measure progress;\nc2/c4/c5 pass vacuously because a checker that detects nothing is silent.\n\n\nForward may-analysis over the MIR CFG keyed on **SymbolId**. Two halves:\n(1) a RECORDER in `HirToMirContext` during lowering appending\n`Bind|Move|Read` events per (function, block) with the HirExpr SourceLocation —\nrecording at lowering time means the SymbolId is in hand, so it needs neither\n`byte_offset` on IrSourceLocation nor `register_to_symbol` (empty on the live\npath); (2) a CHECKER at the tail of `lower_hir_to_mir`, worklist in reverse\npostorder, building its own predecessor map from `successors()` because cached\n`block.predecessors` goes stale.\nLattice per binding: `{live, moved, witness}`; join = OR on the booleans, MIN on\nthe witness by (block, seq) — \"first seen\" is NOT monotone and can oscillate.\n`Bind` KILLS (that is the revive mechanism); `Move` CHECKS THEN SETS (that is\nwhat makes `f(a); g(a)` fire); fixpoint first, report second.\nEnrolment at RECORD time via `derive_move_classes` minus `derive_shared_classes`\n⇒ unannotated legacy Haxe records nothing at all = the silence guarantee.\nKNOWN GAP the design verified: a `@:move` class in an IMPORTED file emits ZERO\nmove opcodes today (`derive_move_classes` is per-context) — fix by NAME, never\nSymbolId.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_ownership_analysis_never_runs` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}